# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts MUST be LF. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named "/bin/bash\r", which fails as
# "cannot execute: required file not found" — a message that points at
# everything except the real cause. It cost a failed production deploy, and
# it also shipped a CRLF install.sh to every macOS and Linux user, where
# `curl … | sh` chokes on the carriage returns.
#
# Without this file, git on Windows converts on checkout and the corrupted
# copy is what gets tarred to the server and baked into the image.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# PowerShell is a Windows citizen; CRLF is its native habit and `irm | iex`
# is happy either way.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
